<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P46597">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_6fc8ba9fcb2a29e89bdf676873fe4234" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_bb3c10eb408391799b14419de79cc473" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acetylserotonin O-methyltransferase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_ASMT_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P46597" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ASMT_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.1.1.4</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Hydroxyindole O-methyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ASMT</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HIOMT</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ASMT_HUMAN Reviewed; 345 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference117438</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P46597_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Isoform 1 catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group ontoN-acetylserotonin, producing melatonin (N-acetyl-5-methoxytryptamine). Isoform 2 and isoform 3 lack enzyme activity.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:22775292}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=N-acetylserotonin + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = H(+) +melatonin + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:15573,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:16796, ChEBI:CHEBI:17697,ChEBI:CHEBI:57856, ChEBI:CHEBI:59789; EC=2.1.1.4;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:22775292};PATHWAY: Aromatic compound metabolism; melatonin biosynthesis;melatonin from serotonin: step 1/2.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22775292}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=P46597-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P46597-2; Sequence=VSP_004285;Name=3;IsoId=P46597-3; Sequence=VSP_004284;Note=Includes part of a LINE-1 element. Ref.1(AAA58582/AAA58583/AAA75290), Ref.2 (AAA17020) and Ref.3(BAG37430) sequences are in conflict in position: 190:W-&gt;R.{ECO:0000305};TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in the pineal gland (at proteinlevel). In the retina, very low expression is found at the mRNAlevel (PubMed:7989373), and not at the protein level(PubMed:8574683). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22775292,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7989373, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8574683}.INDUCTION: By all-trans-, 9-cis- and 13-cis-retinoic acid and byserum treatment, following starvation, in the retinoblastoma cellline Y79. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:8752109,ECO:0000269|PubMed:8842389}.MISCELLANEOUS: The gene coding for this protein is located in thepseudoautosomal region 1 (PAR1) of X and Y chromosomes.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class I-like SAM-bindingmethyltransferase superfamily. Cation-independent O-methyltransferase family. {ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU01020}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Wikipedia; Note=5-hydroxyindole-O-methyltransferase entry;URL=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5-hydroxyindole-O-methyltransferase&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

