<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q8TDX5">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2-amino-3-carboxymuconate-6-semialdehyde decarboxylase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q8TDX5" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_ACMSD_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACMSD_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">4.1.1.45</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Picolinate carboxylase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACMSD</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference115933</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACMSD_HUMAN Reviewed; 336 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Converts alpha-amino-beta-carboxymuconate-epsilon-semialdehyde (ACMS) to alpha-aminomuconate semialdehyde (AMS).ACMS can be converted non-enzymatically to quinolate (QA), a keyprecursor of NAD, and a potent endogenous excitotoxin of neuronalcells which is implicated in the pathogenesis of variousneurodegenerative disorders. In the presence of ACMSD, ACMS isconverted to AMS, a benign catabolite. ACMSD ultimately controlsthe metabolic fate of tryptophan catabolism along the kynureninepathway. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19843166}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2-amino-3-carboxymuconate 6-semialdehyde + H(+) = 2-aminomuconate 6-semialdehyde + CO2; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16557,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:16526, ChEBI:CHEBI:77634,ChEBI:CHEBI:77803; EC=4.1.1.45;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12140278};PATHWAY: Secondary metabolite metabolism; quinolate metabolism.{ECO:0000305|PubMed:12140278}.SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19843166}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1 {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12140278};IsoId=Q8TDX5-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2 {ECO:0000305};IsoId=Q8TDX5-2; Sequence=VSP_050622, VSP_050623;Note=No experimental confirmation available. {ECO:0000305};SIMILARITY: Belongs to the metallo-dependent hydrolasessuperfamily. ACMSD family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q8TDX5-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_612199</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q8TDX5_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_12326_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

